    riskNarr:{security:'ISO 27001 is in place with no public breach on record; SOC 2 depth and the residency Statement-of-Applicability mapping are the open confirmations, requiring a formal screen before award if pursued. A half-step behind Nimbus on certification.',financial:'The strongest financial position in the field: a late-stage, exceptionally well-capitalized platform (~$2.4–3.0B run-rate, multi-$B raised) on an illustrative external read (public sources · not validated). Financial-stability risk is the lowest of the three.',lockin:'Platform breadth invites consolidation onto one vendor; open table formats help portability in principle, but exit terms and ecosystem concentration still need to be pinned down.',geo:'US and EU regions are available and sub-processor jurisdictions are limited; residency posture is straightforward to confirm.',support:'Enterprise support is solid; confirm 24x7 coverage and incident-response RCA depth for a global estate.'},
    riskSubNarr:{security:{rs_breach:'No public breach on record, but a broader multi-workload platform surface carries marginally more residual exposure than a pure warehouse.',rs_cert:'ISO 27001 is in place; SOC 2 Type II depth and the residency SoA mapping are unconfirmed, keeping certification a half-step behind the lead.',rs_vuln:'Vulnerability and pen-test cadence is adequate but spans a wider attack surface (BI + ML), so residual risk is a touch higher.',rs_res:'US and EU regions exist; the SoA-to-Lilly-controls mapping for residency is the open confirmation requiring a formal screen before award.'},financial:{rf_scale:'Revenue at a multi-$B run-rate growing 50–60% (illustrative · external · not validated), the strongest scale story in the field.',rf_runway:'Exceptionally well-capitalized (multi-$B raised) with ample runway; profitability risk is minimal.',rf_owner:'Backed by top-tier institutional investors; ownership is stable ahead of an eventual IPO.'},lockin:{rl_portab:'Open table formats materially help portability in principle, lowering format lock-in below the lead, but the benefit depends on how open the deployment stays in practice.',rl_exit:'Exit and data-egress terms still need to be pinned down; platform breadth raises switching cost despite the open format.',rl_ecosystem:'The platform invites consolidating BI and ML onto one vendor, the field-high ecosystem-concentration risk.'},geo:{rg_region:'Broad US and EU region coverage over Lilly footprint; minimal risk.',rg_subproc:'Sub-processor jurisdictions are limited and disclosed; a small exposure.',rg_reg:'No adverse regulatory exposure identified, a low band.'},support:{rp_sla:'Enterprise SLA guarantees are solid; specific credits to be confirmed in the schedule.',rp_cover:'24x7 coverage is offered; validate global follow-the-sun depth for the Lilly estate.',rp_ir:'Incident-response and RCA are documented; confirm RCA turnaround commitments.'}},
