     reqNarr:{functional:'Strong dimensional and semi-structured modeling plus native ML/data-science on the same governed platform, the capability the lead bidder lacks first-party. Self-service BI is solid if a step behind a pure warehouse UI. The broadest functional footprint in the field.',integration:'Open table formats and a mature API surface give the best portability story, with a broad connector ecosystem including workable SAP paths. The architecture is cloud-native and proven. Integration is a genuine strength, offset only by a steeper operational model.',security:'ISO 27001 is in place and encryption and access controls are sound; SOC 2 depth and the residency Statement-of-Applicability mapping to Lilly controls are the open confirmations. Certification is solid but a half-step behind Nimbus. Would require a formal screen for the SoA check before award.',scale:'Elastic and proven at scale across mixed BI and ML workloads, with strong throughput and concurrency. Latency is competitive. Scales comfortably to the RFP envelope.',governance:'A unified catalog and lineage span BI and ML on one governed copy of data, the strongest governance model in the field for regulated analytics. Fine-grained access and policy management are mature. This is where the lakehouse leads.',commercial:'Capability-per-dollar is competitive, but a higher ramp and implementation cost mean the first-year TCO must absorb an operational learning curve. Enterprise-agreement flexibility is moderate. The weakest category on paper, driven by ramp cost rather than list price.'},
     reqSubNarr:{functional:{fx_model:'Strong dimensional and semi-structured modeling native to the open table formats; only marginally off full marks versus a purpose-built warehouse UI.',fx_etl:'Mature batch and streaming ingestion and transformation on one platform; held just off top by a steeper operational setup than a dedicated ELT stack.',fx_bi:'Self-service BI is capable but the analyst experience trails a pure warehouse front end, which is the deduction here.',fx_ml:'First-party ML and data-science run on the same governed data copy, the exact capability the lead bidder serves only through partners; near the field ceiling.',fx_road:'Well-funded roadmap backed by multi-billion raised with broad extensibility; kept a touch off full marks as breadth adds delivery complexity.'},integration:{in_arch:'Cloud-native elastic lakehouse proven at scale; off full marks only because the unified BI-plus-ML architecture carries a steeper operational model.',in_api:'Mature API surface spanning data and ML workflows; a step short of top pending confirmation of coverage depth across every RFP source.',in_conn:'Broad connector ecosystem covers the RFP sources, but a few sources still need connector validation, keeping it off full marks.',in_sap:'SAP extraction works through the connector ecosystem and is better-proven than the lead path, yet legacy SAP stays the softest integration point.',in_open:'Open table formats give the field-best portability story; just off top since the benefit depends on how open the deployment stays in practice.'},security:{se_enc:'Strong encryption at rest and in transit; a shade off top only because the broader BI-plus-ML surface widens the attack area slightly.',se_soc2:'SOC 2 posture is credible but the Type II scope for Lilly is still being confirmed, which is the deduction here.',se_iso:'ISO 27001 certified with good scope (public sources, not validated); near full marks pending the Statement-of-Applicability mapping to Lilly controls.',se_res:'US and EU regions exist, but the residency Statement-of-Applicability mapping to Lilly controls is unconfirmed and would require a formal screen before award.',se_sso:'SSO and Entra access control are enterprise-grade; held off top pending confirmation against Lilly identity standards.',se_audit:'Audit logging and monitoring span BI and ML, though the wider platform surface leaves more to evidence for full marks.'},scale:{sc_thru:'High query throughput proven across mixed BI and ML workloads; among the field leaders and only marginally off full marks.',sc_conc:'Strong workload isolation holds under concurrent mixed load; a fraction off top on multi-tenant proof at Lilly scale.',sc_elastic:'Compute and storage separation scales cleanly and elastically; near the field ceiling for the RFP envelope.',sc_latency:'Latency is competitive at RFP scale but trails a pure warehouse on interactive query, the reason for the deduction.'},governance:{gv_catalog:'Unified catalog spans BI and ML on one governed copy, the strongest catalog model in the field; just off full marks.',gv_lineage:'End-to-end column and row lineage across both workloads; a step short of top pending demonstration at Lilly regulated-data scope.',gv_access:'Fine-grained access and masking are mature; off top as policy depth for regulated employee and clinical data still needs proving.',gv_policy:'Policy and classification management is well-developed, but the broader platform scope leaves more to validate for full marks.'},commercial:{cm_license:'Capacity-plus-consumption unit economics at roughly 2.95M per year committed-use per cluster sit below the field on list value, dropping under the adequacy bar.',cm_impl:'The weak point: a higher ramp and enablement cost than a pure warehouse drags first-year TCO well below adequate.',cm_run:'Run cost is moderate but the lakehouse operational learning curve adds ongoing overhead, keeping it just under threshold.',cm_flex:'The enterprise agreement with committed capacity limits contract and exit flexibility, holding it below the bar.',cm_discount:'Committed-use discounting exists but is less aggressive than the value challenger, leaving it under threshold.'}},
